## 📦 Enable Dynamic Persistent Volumes in `kind` using Local Path Provisioner

`local-path-provisioner` enables dynamic provisioning of PersistentVolumes using local disk paths (`hostPath`)—perfect for local clusters like `kind` running on Docker or EC2.

---

### ✅ Why Use It?

- No need to manually create PVs
- Ideal for local development and testing with Stateful apps like MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, etc.
- Automatically provisions `hostPath` volumes per PVC
- Works out of the box with `kind`, `minikube`, and other bare-metal clusters

---

### 🚀 1. Install Local Path Provisioner

```bash
kubectl apply -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rancher/local-path-provisioner/master/deploy/local-path-storage.yaml
```

---

### ⚙️ 2. Set It as the Default StorageClass

```bash
kubectl patch storageclass local-path \
  -p '{"metadata": {"annotations":{"storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class":"true"}}}'
```

✅ This ensures that PVCs without an explicit `storageClassName` will automatically use `local-path`.

---

### 📁 3. Verify Installation

```bash
kubectl get storageclass
```

Expected output:

```
NAME          PROVISIONER                   DEFAULT
local-path    rancher.io/local-path         Yes
```

---

### 📦 4. Use It in Your Deployments or StatefulSets

When creating a `PersistentVolumeClaim` or using `volumeClaimTemplates` in a `StatefulSet`, set the storage class like this:

```yaml
storageClassName: local-path
```

Kubernetes will automatically:
- Create the PVC
- Dynamically provision a matching PV using `hostPath`

✅ No need to manually define PV or PVC YAML files!

---

### 🔍 5. Verify PVC and PV Binding

```bash
kubectl get pvc -A
kubectl get pv
```

You should see PVCs in the `Bound` state and dynamically provisioned PVs.

---

### 📂 6. Default Volume Path on the Host

By default, volumes are stored in:

```
/opt/local-path-provisioner/
```

Each dynamically provisioned volume will be created in:

```
/opt/local-path-provisioner/pvc-<unique-id>/
```

---

### 🧹 7. Uninstall Local Path Provisioner (if needed)

```bash
kubectl delete -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rancher/local-path-provisioner/master/deploy/local-path-storage.yaml
```

---

### ✅ Summary

| Feature                          | Supported |
|----------------------------------|-----------|
| Dynamic volume provisioning      | ✅ Yes     |
| Manual PV creation required      | ❌ No      |
| Supports StatefulSets            | ✅ Yes     |
| Works on kind, EC2, bare-metal   | ✅ Yes     |
| Uses hostPath under the hood     | ✅ Yes     |

---

ℹ️ **Pro Tip**: Use `local-path-provisioner` to simulate cloud-like dynamic volume behavior in local Kubernetes environments such as `kind`, `minikube`, or bare-metal clusters.
